From: TNG Technical Manual compatibility investigation
Subject: [PATCH] DIRECTOR: Accept TrekTech factory put sentinel argument

The credits hotspot table is populated through a Director 3 factory object.
Its crew-name entries call mPut with key, value, and a trailing zero sentinel,
while the normal location entries use only key and value.  Director accepts
the unused trailing argument, but ScummVM currently treats it as the value and
the caption text as the key, leaving every credits name absent from the table.

For TrekTech only, discard the single surplus trailing argument to the factory
put method and retain the existing strict argument checks everywhere else.
---
 engines/director/lingo/lingo-code.cpp | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/engines/director/lingo/lingo-code.cpp b/engines/director/lingo/lingo-code.cpp
--- a/engines/director/lingo/lingo-code.cpp
+++ b/engines/director/lingo/lingo-code.cpp
@@ -1799,6 +1799,15 @@ void LC::call(const Symbol &funcSym, int nargs, bool allowRetVal) {
 					g_lingo->push(d);
 					nargs++;
 				}
+			} else if (Common::String(g_director->getGameId()).equals("trektech") &&
+					funcSym.type == HBLTIN && target.type == OBJECT &&
+					(target.u.obj->getObjType() & kFactoryObj) && funcSym.name &&
+					funcSym.name->equalsIgnoreCase("put") &&
+					nargs == funcSym.maxArgs + 1) {
+				// TrekTech's credits table supplies an unused trailing zero to mPut.
+				// Director ignores it; remove it before LM::m_put pops value and key.
+				g_lingo->pop();
+				nargs--;
 			}
 		} else if (funcSym.nargs > nargs || funcSym.maxArgs < nargs) {
 			warning("Incorrect number of arguments for builtin '%s' (%d, expected %d to %d). Dropping %d stack items.",
-- 
